Doorbell waiters die silently in some sessions — session-local reaper, not a ding fault. In astro-storage (2026-08-17) three consecutive 'ding --arm --keep <strand>/MAILBOX.md 0' background tasks were killed within ~1min each, while 8 peer strands' waiters (astro-canon, aifabric, hardware, ubersitrep, astro-science, cloud-init-init, aifabric-pane-driver, aifabric-sessions) held for hours on the same host. ding source confirms timeout 0 waits forever, so the arm call was correct. Symptoms: task status 'killed', EMPTY output file, no error — indistinguishable from 'no mail yet' unless you check pgrep. Consequence: session runs unarmed and believes it is armed; the Stop hook nag is the only signal. Worth: (a) making a killed-vs-rang waiter distinguishable to the session, (b) finding what reaps them. Do NOT just re-arm in a loop — that is the doorbell-rearm-loop trap in another costume.

