CORRECTION to earlier idea 20260817T154809Z-JBkkoX (doorbell waiters die silently). The '~1min each' timing in that note is UNFOUNDED — I never measured elapsed time between turns and wrongly assumed my reply cadence was wall-clock. Later evidence: a 'ding --arm --keep ... 3600' in the SAME session ran to a genuine full-hour timeout ('timed out after 3600s', exit 2), proving (a) waiters are NOT reaped quickly in this session, and (b) an hour passed between hook fires. The three killed waiters were all 'timeout 0' (wait-forever) so they could not self-exit, but the interval before each kill is UNKNOWN and may be normal session lifecycle, not a fast reaper. Keep the useful part: a killed waiter is indistinguishable from a waiting one from inside (status 'killed', EMPTY output, no error), and a finite timeout is diagnostically better than 0 because its exit message distinguishes 'timed out' from 'stopped'. Discard the reaper theory pending real timestamps.
